1.BASIC NAVIGATION COMMANDS

pwd _  Displays the current directory
ls _ Lists files and directories
ls -l _ Lists files with details
ls -a _ Shows hidden files
cd directory _ Moves into a directory
cd .. _ Moves to the parent directory
cd ~ _ Moves to the home directory
clear _ Clears the terminal screen


2. FILE AND DIRECTORY COMMANDS

touch file.txt _Creates an empty file
mkdir folder _  Creates a directory
mkdir -p a/b   _Creates nested directories
cp file.txt copy.txt_  Copies a file
mv old.txt new.txt_ Renames or moves a file
rm file.txt_    Deletes a file
rmdir folder_   Removes an empty directory
cat file.txt_   Displays file contents
less file.txt_  Views a file page by page
head file.txt_  Displays the first 10 lines
tail file.txt_  Displays the last 10 lines


3. FILE SEARCH AND TEXT COMMANDS 

find . -name "*.txt"_  Finds text files
grep "error" file.txt _ Searches for a word
wc -l file.txt _ Counts lines
sort file.txt _ Sorts lines
uniq file.txt _ Removes adjacent duplicate lines

4.PERMISSIONS AND USERS

whoami _ Displays the current username
id _ Displays user and group IDs
chmod 755 file.sh_ Changes file permissions
chown user file.txt _ Changes file ownership; may require elevated privileges
sudo command _ Runs a command with elevated privileges
